OL,3,GNEWSA'Pigs Village' Welsh name change
OL,4,Awill go ahead
OL,5,
OL,6,FA rural Welsh village will officially
OL,7,Fchange its name to Pentre Moch -
OL,8,Fliterally translated as Pigs Village.
OL,10,FThe name dates back to at least the
OL,11,F17th Century and referred to the pig
OL,12,Ffarm around which the Flintshire
OL,13,Fvillage of Northop Hall grew.
OL,15,FNorthop Hall will retain its English
OL,16,Fname, but Pentre Moch will become its
OL,17,Fprimary Welsh name following approval
OL,18,Fby Flintshire council.
OL,23,APub: 22-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
